STATUS: Generate one flat, shared parchment backplate for the campaign chapter
selector, using the user-provided campaign-screen screenshot as the visual
reference. Focus only on the grouped chapter controls in the screenshot's
upper-right corner. This is one reusable background asset for all chapter
icons, not a separate parchment card per icon. Do not turn it into a rolled
scroll banner or add large end ornaments.

## Reference input

- Attach the user-provided campaign-screen reference screenshot. Use it to
  match the chapter selector's flat parchment plaque, aged edges, gold trim,
  and compact horizontal proportions.
- Inspect only the upper-right chapter selector as the design reference. Do
  not recreate the screenshot, campaign map, outer map frame, or other UI.
- If available, attach
  `assets_src/campaign/ui/campaign_map_frame_overlay.png` only as a material
  and color reference. The selector panel remains a separate foreground UI
  asset.

## Output

- Generate exactly one PNG:
  `campaign_chapter_selector_parchment.png`.
- Save it under `assets_src/campaign/ui/`.
- Canvas: exactly 1920 × 512 pixels, horizontal, RGBA.
- Keep the canvas transparent outside the single shared panel. Use genuine
  alpha, not a checkerboard or a painted transparent-looking area.
- Create one continuous, shallow rectangular parchment panel with a restrained
  outer border. Do not make a sprite sheet, separate per-chapter cards, or
  multiple variants.
- Keep the center field visually quiet and horizontally stretch-friendly:
  detailed corner/end ornaments stay near the ends, while the central
  parchment texture and border remain simple enough to resize for a variable
  number of chapter tabs.
- Do not add NinePatch guide marks, crop marks, labels, or a background.

## Panel design

- Match the reference's aged parchment face, warm tan/ivory tones, softly
  darkened paper edges, and a narrow, restrained antique-gold edge.
- Keep the panel's silhouette wide and compact, approximately 3.75:1, so it
  reads as one shared selector plaque rather than a full-screen banner.
- Keep the panel flat and plaque-like, with gently worn, shallow edges. Use
  only subtle paper texture and minimal border detail. Do not add rolled ends,
  curled scrolls, side handles, diamond medallions, or prominent ornaments.
  Keep the visual weight below the campaign map's main outer frame; the panel
  must not compete with level markers or the map.
- The same backplate serves every chapter icon, regardless of chapter theme or
  selection state. Do not tint or decorate it differently for Chapter 1,
  Chapter 2, locked chapters, or completed chapters.
- Maintain clear contrast for separate dark live labels and chapter artwork
  placed over the parchment.

## Separation from chapter icons and live UI

- Generate the shared parchment backplate only. The wide chapter-map-preview
  thumbnails remain separate assets described by
  `docs/systems/campaign-chapter-icons.agp`.
- Do not draw individual icon tiles, per-icon parchment backgrounds,
  separators, fixed icon slots, thumbnails, maps, or landscape artwork.
- Do not include chapter numbers, names, text, letters, runes that resemble
  writing, locks, checkmarks, progress indicators, or selection states.
- Do not include the campaign map, its perimeter frame, Back control, Start
  Level button, level markers, fortresses, bosses, characters, or other UI.
- Do not add detached shadows, glow, particles, or decorative elements outside
  the panel silhouette. Do not alter or imply any map-anchor positions.

## Review checklist

- Confirm the output is one 1920 × 512 RGBA PNG with transparent space outside
  the panel.
- Confirm it reads as a single shared parchment background for a horizontal
  group of chapter icons, not multiple individual cards.
- Confirm the center can stretch to support different visible chapter counts
  without distorting detailed ornaments or exposing seams.
- Composite it behind the separate Chapter 1 and Chapter 2 icons from the
  reference; verify both remain readable and the panel does not obscure map
  content or surrounding UI.
- Confirm there is no text, chapter art, status badge, icon, map, or second
  screen element baked into the asset.
- Do not import the generated image into Android until it has been reviewed
  and approved.

## Negative prompt

full campaign screen, screenshot, map, landscape, terrain, route, water, sky,
fortress, boss, level marker, chapter icon, emblem, thumbnail, chapter card,
individual parchment tile, per-icon background, fixed icon slots, divider,
multiple panels, multiple assets, rolled scroll ends, curled scrolls, scroll
handles, large diamond ornaments, side medallions, oversized corner
decorations, text, letters, numbers, runes, labels, chapter title, chapter
number, lock, checkmark, progress bar, selection glow, Back button, Start
Level button, UI controls, opaque canvas, painted transparent-looking area,
checkerboard, detached shadow, detached glow, particles, excessive filigree,
modern plastic, watermark, signature
